From 062cb2cc692117e1cea53094aa2b8efb21a64246 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: testuser <mainta@example.test>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:50:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] fix(llms): drop blank keys from Bedrock tool-use inputs
 on replay

- Add `sdk/packages/llms/src/providers/bedrock-tool-use-input.ts` to remove blank keys.
  Match empty keys and Java whitespace-only keys.
  Remove them at any depth, including inside arrays.
  Keep the original value unchanged.
- Apply cleanup only to Bedrock Converse replay inputs.
  Keep conversation history unchanged.
  Leave Bedrock Mantle and other providers unchanged.
- In two A15 runs on stage direct, GPT-6 Astra returned `run_commands` with the input `{"commands": [...], " ": ""}` on its fourth call.
  Live Converse refuses blank keys on all five supported models, so a model switch cannot help.
- Fix replay rejection at `messages.7.content.0.toolUse.input`.
  Bedrock accepted the model response but rejected its blank key during replay.
- Keep accepted keys unchanged.
  Preserve AI SDK Bedrock provider 5.0.98's `{rawInvalidInput}` behavior.
- Pass 47 new tests across two files.
  These include 12 unit tests and 35 wire tests.
  Before the change, 15 wire tests failed.
  The unit file could not load.
- Pass build:sdk, llms, core, shared, agents, cli, and types gates.
  Passing counts: llms 1258, core 3063, shared 485, agents 157, cli 1338.
  Biome check is clean on touched files.
- Live replay failed 2 of 2 without the change.
  Live replay passed 6 of 6 with the change.
- The arm64 binary is not rebuilt or promoted.
  The patch moves the worker image key.
  It joins a later image batch.
